# Regression coverage for `bool` comparisons over partially matched vectors.
# The `bool` modifier changes the output of matched pairs (0/1 instead of
# filtering), but unmatched vector elements must still be omitted from the
# result — they are never synthesized as 0.
#
# The vendored operators.test never exercises this: its bool cases use a
# single series per side, so an absent RHS sample empties the whole RHS
# vector and short-circuits before matching. Here the RHS is non-empty but
# matches only one of the two LHS series.

load 5m
  left_side{env="prod"}  5 5
  left_side{env="dev"}   2 2
  right_side{env="prod"} 3 3

# prod matches and compares true -> 1; dev has no RHS match -> omitted.
eval instant at 5m left_side > bool right_side
  {env="prod"} 1

# prod matches and compares false -> 0 (bool keeps matched-false results);
# dev still has no RHS match -> omitted, not 0.
eval instant at 5m left_side < bool right_side
  {env="prod"} 0

# Same shape with on(env) matching must agree with the unmodified form.
eval instant at 5m left_side > bool on(env) right_side
  {env="prod"} 1

clear
